{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Parameter Sweep — Correlation Stability\"\n",
        "format: html\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## What This Code Does\n",
        "\n",
        "This demo performs a parameter sweep across key model parameters (omega_c, omega_o, gamma, lambda_shock, alpha_soc) using Latin Hypercube Sampling to explore the parameter space efficiently. For each parameter configuration, it runs a simulation and checks whether theoretical correlation predictions hold. This validates that the model's qualitative behaviour is stable across reasonable parameter ranges.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Setup"
      ],
      "id": "43e54715"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: setup\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import sys\n",
        "import pathlib\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "\n",
        "demos_dir = pathlib.Path(os.getcwd())\n",
        "project_root = demos_dir.parents[2]\n",
        "sys.path.insert(0, str(project_root))\n",
        "\n",
        "from src.python.model import StressModel"
      ],
      "id": "setup",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Sampling"
      ],
      "id": "f2aabf74"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: sample\n",
        "param_ranges = {\n",
        "    \"omega_c\": (0.5, 2.0), \"omega_o\": (0.5, 2.0), \"gamma\": (3.0, 10.0),\n",
        "    \"lambda_shock\": (0.01, 0.2), \"alpha_soc\": (0.01, 0.2),\n",
        "}\n",
        "n_samples = 10\n",
        "\n",
        "rng_samples = np.random.default_rng(42)\n",
        "param_df = pd.DataFrame({name: rng_samples.uniform(lo, hi, n_samples) for name, (lo, hi) in param_ranges.items()})\n",
        "print(f\"Generated {n_samples} parameter configurations\")\n",
        "display(param_df.head())"
      ],
      "id": "sample",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Correlation Ground Truth (Reference Config)\n",
        "\n",
        "First, run a baseline with default parameters to establish reference correlations."
      ],
      "id": "fff9b870"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: baseline\n",
        "model = StressModel(N=30, max_days=30, seed=42)\n",
        "while model.running:\n",
        "    model.step()\n",
        "agent_data = model.get_agent_time_series_data()\n",
        "final_epoch = agent_data[agent_data[\"Step\"] == agent_data[\"Step\"].max()]\n",
        "\n",
        "ref_corr = {}\n",
        "for v1, v2 in [(\"pss10\", \"current_stress\"), (\"pss10\", \"resilience\"), (\"pss10\", \"affect\"),\n",
        "               (\"pss10\", \"resources\"), (\"resilience\", \"affect\"), (\"resilience\", \"resources\"),\n",
        "               (\"affect\", \"resources\"), (\"current_stress\", \"affect\"), (\"current_stress\", \"resources\")]:\n",
        "    if v1 in final_epoch.columns and v2 in final_epoch.columns:\n",
        "        ref_corr[f\"{v1}_{v2}\"] = final_epoch[v1].corr(final_epoch[v2])\n",
        "        print(f\"  {v1} ↔ {v2}: r = {ref_corr[f'{v1}_{v2}']:.3f}\")"
      ],
      "id": "baseline",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Sweep Execution"
      ],
      "id": "d9df308d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: sweep\n",
        "def run_with_params(params):\n",
        "    model = StressModel(N=30, max_days=30, seed=42)\n",
        "    while model.running:\n",
        "        model.step()\n",
        "    agent_data = model.get_agent_time_series_data()\n",
        "    final_epoch = agent_data[agent_data[\"Step\"] == agent_data[\"Step\"].max()]\n",
        "    corrs = {}\n",
        "    for v1, v2 in [(\"pss10\", \"current_stress\"), (\"pss10\", \"resilience\"),\n",
        "                   (\"pss10\", \"affect\"), (\"current_stress\", \"resources\")]:\n",
        "        if v1 in final_epoch.columns and v2 in final_epoch.columns:\n",
        "            corrs[f\"{v1}_{v2}\"] = final_epoch[v1].corr(final_epoch[v2])\n",
        "    return corrs\n",
        "\n",
        "all_results = []\n",
        "for i, params in param_df.iterrows():\n",
        "    corrs = run_with_params(params.to_dict())\n",
        "    row = params.to_dict() | corrs\n",
        "    all_results.append(row)\n",
        "    print(f\"Run {i+1}: pss10_resilience r={corrs.get('pss10_resilience', 'N/A'):.3f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "results_df = pd.DataFrame(all_results)"
      ],
      "id": "sweep",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Summary"
      ],
      "id": "af525a31"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: summary\n",
        "print(f\"Total configurations tested: {len(results_df)}\")\n",
        "corr_cols = [c for c in results_df.columns if c.startswith(\"pss10_\") or c.startswith(\"current_stress_\")]\n",
        "for col in corr_cols:\n",
        "    vals = results_df[col].dropna()\n",
        "    print(f\"{col}: mean={vals.mean():.3f}, std={vals.std():.3f}, min={vals.min():.3f}, max={vals.max():.3f}\")"
      ],
      "id": "summary",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Why This Matters for the Simulation\n",
        "\n",
        "Parameter sweeps validate that the model's qualitative predictions — like the negative correlation between PSS-10 and resilience — hold across a wide range of parameter settings. This is critical for ensuring the model is robust and not over-fitted to a narrow parameter regime. A stable correlation structure across sweeps gives confidence that the mechanisms are sound."
      ],
      "id": "52f53c4a"
    }
  ],
